#: includes/class-bsms-rest.php:2875
#: includes/class-bsms-rest.php:2882
msgid "Sending SMS"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bsms-rest.php:2876
msgid "Why did a message fail?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bsms-rest.php:2876
msgid "The usual reasons are a wrong or switched-off phone number, a number on the Do Not Disturb list, or a sender name the network does not accept. Open Message History and tap the message to see the reason. The charge for a failed message is returned to your wallet."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bsms-rest.php:2876
msgid "Delivery & DND"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bsms-rest.php:2877
msgid "I paid but my wallet has not changed"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bsms-rest.php:2877
msgid "Online payments are added straight away. If you paid by bank transfer, we check your receipt first, which can take a little while during working hours. You can see where your transfer is on the Buy SMS page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bsms-rest.php:2877
#: includes/class-bsms-rest.php:2883
msgid "Funding & Wallet"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bsms-rest.php:2878
msgid "Why can’t I use my sender name?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bsms-rest.php:2878
msgid "A sender name can be used once it has been approved. While it is waiting, it will not appear on the Send SMS page. If it was not approved, the Sender ID page shows the reason and you can ask for a different name."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bsms-rest.php:2879
msgid "Why is my API request failing?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bsms-rest.php:2879
msgid "Check the API key, the web address, the sender name, the phone number format and the wallet balance. The response code in the reply tells you which one to fix."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bsms-rest.php:2879
#: includes/class-bsms-rest.php:2885
msgid "API & Integrations"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bsms-rest.php:2882
msgid "Understand message results"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bsms-rest.php:2882
msgid "What Successful, Failed, Sending and Not sent mean."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bsms-rest.php:2882
msgid "Successful means the network accepted your message and did not report a failure. Failed means it could not be delivered, and its charge is returned to your wallet, even if the failure is reported later. Sending means it has not reached the network yet, or was sent a short while ago. Not sent means it was left out, for example a repeated or wrong number, and it was not charged. Each message has a message ID you can quote to support."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bsms-rest.php:2883
msgid "How your wallet works"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bsms-rest.php:2883
msgid "Add money once, then pay for each SMS as you send."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bsms-rest.php:2883
msgid "Money you add on the Buy SMS page goes into your wallet. Each SMS you send takes its charge from the wallet. Online payments are added straight away; bank transfers are added once we have checked the receipt."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bsms-rest.php:2884
msgid "Getting a sender name approved"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bsms-rest.php:2884
msgid "Ask for the name people see when you text them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bsms-rest.php:2884
msgid "Use your real business, school or church name, up to 11 letters or numbers. Add a sample of the messages you will send. Names that look like a bank, a network or a government office are usually not approved."
msgstr ""

